WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:08.148
Kubernetes deployment scripts are
security-relevant operational automation.

2
00:00:08.228 --> 00:00:15.654
Before applying changes, validate the
cluster context, namespace, workload,

3
00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:18.284
release, and environment.

4
00:00:18.364 --> 00:00:24.903
Do not rely on an accidental active
context on a workstation or runner.

5
00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:32.077
Development, staging, and production
should have separate expectations,

6
00:00:32.157 --> 00:00:36.369
credentials, policies, and approval paths.

7
00:00:36.449 --> 00:00:43.986
Use scoped identities and RBAC rather than
broad cluster administrator access.

8
00:00:44.066 --> 00:00:50.495
Protect kubeconfig files, service-account
tokens, CI/CD secrets,

9
00:00:50.575 --> 00:00:52.791
and runner identities.

10
00:00:52.871 --> 00:00:58.635
Separate validation, apply, rollback,
secret-management,

11
00:00:58.715 --> 00:01:03.592
and administrative capabilities where
practical.

12
00:01:03.672 --> 00:01:11.542
Review, rotate, and revoke deployment
credentials over time so old automation does

13
00:01:11.622 --> 00:01:14.393
not become forgotten access.

14
00:01:14.473 --> 00:01:20.790
Invoke kubectl, Helm, Kustomize, and
supporting tools with fixed,

15
00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:23.420
reviewable Bash patterns.

16
00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:30.815
Validate names, namespaces, file paths,
chart names, release names, images,

17
00:01:30.895 --> 00:01:32.225
and timeouts.

18
00:01:32.305 --> 00:01:37.736
Control working directories and expected
tool versions.

19
00:01:37.816 --> 00:01:42.804
Review rendered output before high-impact
applies,

20
00:01:42.884 --> 00:01:46.874
use diffs to understand intended changes,

21
00:01:46.954 --> 00:01:53.161
and connect approved changes to versioned
deployment artifacts.

22
00:01:53.241 --> 00:02:00.668
Finally, control images, configuration,
and secrets; verify rollout health;

23
00:02:00.748 --> 00:02:06.179
plan rollback; log safely; monitor
unexpected behavior;

24
00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:11.136
and review deployment scripts and access
over time.

25
00:02:11.216 --> 00:02:16.093
A good deployment script does more than
apply files.

26
00:02:16.173 --> 00:02:23.266
It makes the deployment scoped,
least-privileged, reviewed, observable,

27
00:02:23.346 --> 00:02:27.780
verifiable, recoverable, and safe to
operate.
